          {
            title: 'King',
            subtitle: 'Compendium',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'King is a compendium card game played in many countries including Belgium, Italy, Portugal, Russia, Turkey, Colombia, and Brazil. Despite its English name, there is no evidence it was ever played in English-speaking countries. The game consists of a series of rounds with different objectivesâ€”some negative (avoiding specific cards or tricks) and some positive (winning tricks). It is closely related to Barbu, Kierki, and Trex.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "The game is known by the English name 'King' in many non-English speaking countries, leading to speculation about English origins. However, no evidence exists of it being played in English-speaking countries. It likely evolved from European compendium games in the early 20th century.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
