        'Early 1900s: Game emerges in various European and South American countries',
        'Mid-20th century: Standardized versions appear in Belgium (Kingen), Russia, and Turkey (RÄ±fkÄ±)',
        '1970s: Spreads to Colombia and Brazil',
        'Present: Remains popular in social clubs and cafes across multiple countries',
      ],
      evolution: 'Each region developed slight variations. The Belgian version (Kingen) became the basis for the international game Barbu. Turkish King (RÄ±fkÄ±) and Russian King have distinct local rules.',
